        }
      ],
      "text": "@joshelman 🙏 I am thankful of the respect of honest critics!",
      "url": "https://x.com/alexandr_wang/status/1467715471050883076"
    },
    {
      "author_id": "615818451",
      "created_at": "2021-12-06T03:41:19.000Z",
      "edit_history_tweet_ids": [
        "1467700655045238785"
      ],
      "id": "1467700655045238785",
      "in_reply_to_user_id": "615818451",
      "public_metrics": {
        "bookmark_count": 9,
        "impression_count": 0,
        "like_count": 173,
        "quote_count": 1,
        "reply_count": 3,
        "retweet_count": 6
      },
      "referenced_tweets": [
        {
          "id": "1467700654223233026",
          "type": "replied_to"
        }
      ],
      "text": "This means we’re going to see an even greater structural repricing of nerds—more than we’ve already seen.\n\nNerds are becoming more and more important, and funnily enough, becoming cool in the process.\n\n9/n",
      "url": "https://x.com/alexandr_wang/status/1467700655045238785"
    },
    {
      "author_id": "615818451",
      "created_at": "2021-12-06T03:41:19.000Z",
      "edit_history_tweet_ids": [
        "1467700654223233026"
      ],
      "id": "1467700654223233026",
      "in_reply_to_user_id": "615818451",
      "public_metrics": {
        "bookmark_count": 6,
        "impression_count": 0,
        "like_count": 82,
        "quote_count": 4,
        "reply_count": 2,
        "retweet_count": 2
      },
      "referenced_tweets": [
        {
          "id": "1467700653329842182",
          "type": "replied_to"
        }
      ],
      "text": "They can even distribute without the cool kids now through the internet.\n\nMeme culture is nerd culture gone cool, and has empowered the nerd to distribute far more scalable than even the cool kids.\n\n8/n",
      "url": "https://x.com/alexandr_wang/status/1467700654223233026"
    },
    {
      "author_id": "615818451",
      "created_at": "2021-12-06T03:41:18.000Z",
      "edit_history_tweet_ids": [
        "1467700653329842182"
      ],
      "id": "1467700653329842182",
      "in_reply_to_user_id": "615818451",
      "public_metrics": {
        "bookmark_count": 4,
        "impression_count": 0,
        "like_count": 102,
        "quote_count": 1,
        "reply_count": 1,
        "retweet_count": 7
      },
      "referenced_tweets": [
        {
          "id": "1467700652499365888",
          "type": "replied_to"
        }
      ],
      "text": "What that means is the nerds are significantly more powerful today than ever before.\n\nThey always could build, but now they can get capital just by appealing to other nerds. They could always do this at a small scale (seed funding), but now you can get $B’s from other nerds.\n\n7/n",
      "url": "https://x.com/alexandr_wang/status/1467700653329842182"
    },
    {
      "author_id": "615818451",
      "created_at": "2021-12-06T03:41:18.000Z",
      "edit_history_tweet_ids": [
        "1467700652499365888"
      ],
      "id": "1467700652499365888",
      "in_reply_to_user_id": "615818451",
      "public_metrics": {
        "bookmark_count": 5,
        "impression_count": 0,
        "like_count": 92,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "reply_count": 2,
        "retweet_count": 4
      },
      "referenced_tweets": [
        {
          "id": "1467700651626926082",
          "type": "replied_to"
        }
      ],
      "text": "Over the past 2 decades, the nerds have steadily accumulated more and more capital, to which they now rival the cool kids.\n\nCrypto was one of the biggest shifts here, where nerds have almost exclusively accumulated $2T in capital.\n\n6/n",
      "url": "https://x.com/alexandr_wang/status/1467700652499365888"
    },
    {
      "author_id": "615818451",
      "created_at": "2021-12-06T03:41:18.000Z",
      "edit_history_tweet_ids": [
        "1467700651626926082"
      ],
      "id": "1467700651626926082",
      "in_reply_to_user_id": "615818451",
      "public_metrics": {
        "bookmark_count": 1,
        "impression_count": 0,
        "like_count": 63,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "reply_count": 1,
        "retweet_count": 3
      },
      "referenced_tweets": [
        {
          "id": "1467700650850992128",
          "type": "replied_to"
        }
      ],
      "text": "That meant cool kids were necessary to get money. Fundraising, enterprise sales, big deals. All of those things required cool kids, which put nerds in the back seat.\n\n5/n",
      "url": "https://x.com/alexandr_wang/status/1467700651626926082"
    },
    {
      "author_id": "615818451",
      "created_at": "2021-12-06T03:41:18.000Z",
      "edit_history_tweet_ids": [
        "1467700650850992128"
      ],
      "id": "1467700650850992128",
      "in_reply_to_user_id": "615818451",
      "public_metrics": {
        "bookmark_count": 3,
        "impression_count": 0,
        "like_count": 63,
        "quote_count": 2,
        "reply_count": 3,
        "retweet_count": 3
      },
      "referenced_tweets": [
        {
          "id": "1467700649995345920",
          "type": "replied_to"
        }
      ],
      "text": "It also used to be that the cool kids were the rich kids. Obviously our recent era is full of counter examples (Gates, Zuck, etc.).\n\nBut for the most part, cool kids controlled most of the capital.\n\n4/n",
      "url": "https://x.com/alexandr_wang/status/1467700650850992128"
    },
    {
      "author_id": "615818451",
      "created_at": "2021-12-06T03:41:18.000Z",
      "edit_history_tweet_ids": [
        "1467700649995345920"
      ],
      "id": "1467700649995345920",
      "in_reply_to_user_id": "615818451",
      "public_metrics": {
        "bookmark_count": 11,
        "impression_count": 0,
        "like_count": 110,
        "quote_count": 1,
        "reply_count": 1,
        "retweet_count": 5
      },
      "referenced_tweets": [
        {
          "id": "1467700649177485316",
          "type": "replied_to"
        }
      ],
      "text": "In business, cool kids and nerds each play their respective roles.\n\nNerds build. Their superpower is building really cool stuff with the latest tech.\n\nCool kids distribute. Their superpower is telling the world in a relatable way, and getting people excited about it.\n\n3/n",
      "url": "https://x.com/alexandr_wang/status/1467700649995345920"
    },
    {
      "author_id": "615818451",
      "created_at": "2021-12-06T03:41:17.000Z",
      "edit_history_tweet_ids": [
        "1467700649177485316"
      ],
      "id": "1467700649177485316",
      "in_reply_to_user_id": "615818451",
      "public_metrics": {
        "bookmark_count": 7,
        "impression_count": 0,
        "like_count": 95,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "reply_count": 1,
        "retweet_count": 4
      },
      "referenced_tweets": [
        {
          "id": "1467700647092916224",
          "type": "replied_to"
        }
      ],
      "text": "It’s not totally true the cool kids don’t build. The nerds build things and the cool kids build relationships.\n\nNerds are jealous of the connectivity, cool kids are jealous of the substance\n\n2/n",
      "url": "https://x.com/alexandr_wang/status/1467700649177485316"
    },
    {
      "author_id": "615818451",
      "created_at": "2021-12-06T03:41:17.000Z",
      "edit_history_tweet_ids": [
        "1467700647092916224"
      ],
      "id": "1467700647092916224",
      "public_metrics": {
        "bookmark_count": 331,
        "impression_count": 0,
        "like_count": 713,
        "quote_count": 60,
        "reply_count": 30,
        "retweet_count": 103
      },
      "text": "The nerds vs the cool kids, a short thread 🧵 \n\nThe nerds are jealous of the cool kids for being, well, cool.\n\nThe cool kids are jealous of the nerds for the ability to build.\n\n1/n",
      "url": "https://x.com/alexandr_wang/status/1467700647092916224"
    },
